"/w/images/thumb/3/32/Stunned_Condition_Icon.webp/25px-Stunned_Condition_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/3/32/Stunned_Condition_Icon.webp/38px-Stunned_Condition_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/3/32/Stunned_Condition_Icon.webp/50px-Stunned_Condition_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Stunned Condition Icon.webp\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/3/32/Stunned_Condition_Icon.webp/25px-Stunned_Condition_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/3/32/Stunned_Condition_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></div></td><td class=\"mbox-text\"><div class=\"mbox-text-span\">This is a disambiguation page, which links to ambiguously named articles. If you were <a href=\"/wiki/Special:WhatLinksHere/Adamantine\" title=\"Special:WhatLinksHere/Adamantine\">brought here</a> by a link in an article, consider editing it to direct towards the intended page instead.</div></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><b>Adamantine</b> is a rare metal known for its unrivaled hardness, and appears in the game as the item <a href=\"/wiki/Adamantine_Slag\" title=\"Adamantine Slag\">Adamantine Slag</a>. The location <a href=\"/wiki/Adamantine_Forge_(location)\" title=\"Adamantine Forge (location)\">Adamantine Forge</a> is named after the metal, as is the <a href=\"/wiki/Adamantine_Forge_(quest)\" title=\"Adamantine Forge (quest)\">similarly named quest</a>, which involves the creation of <a href=\"/wiki/Adamantine_set\" title=\"Adamantine set\">adamantine equipment</a>, albeit using <a href=\"/wiki/Mithral_Ore\" title=\"Mithral Ore\">Mithral Ore</a>:\n</p>\n<ul><li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-block\" style=\"gap: 6px\"><span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-rare\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Adamantine_Longsword\" title=\"Adamantine Longsword\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/9/92/Ada